  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 104.46 Very poorly drained soils",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 104.46 “Very poorly drained soils” means hydric soils that are flooded daily by tides or soils that have aquic conditions in the upper part and have one or more of the characteristics identified in Env-Wq 1014.03.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19; renumbered by #13945 (formerly Env-Wt 104.45)",
